{"id":"srp-t0-0001","lang":"srp","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.hello","domain":1,"text_native":"Здраво. Zdravo.","text_romanized":"ZDRAH-voh","text_english":"Hello.","source_caption":"Hello.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The default greeting anywhere. Works with every age and every status.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Serbian phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbian_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"srp-t0-0002","lang":"srp","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.morning","domain":1,"text_native":"Добро јутро. Dobro jutro.","text_romanized":"DOH-broh YOO-troh","text_english":"Good morning.","source_caption":"Good morning.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Used until roughly midday. Getting the time of day wrong is noticed; not saying it is only noticed by someone expecting it.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Serbian phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbian_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"srp-t0-0003","lang":"srp","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.afternoon","domain":1,"text_native":"поподне. popodne.","text_romanized":"poh-POHD-neh","text_english":"Good afternoon.","source_caption":"afternoon","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The middle of the day. In several languages this is the same word as the evening greeting, and using it late is not an error.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Serbian phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbian_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"srp-t0-0004","lang":"srp","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.evening","domain":1,"text_native":"Добро вече. Dobro veče.","text_romanized":"DOH-broh VEH-cheh","text_english":"Good evening.","source_caption":"Good evening.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"From late afternoon. Often interchangeable with the afternoon greeting.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Serbian phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbian_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"srp-t0-0005","lang":"srp","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.how-are-you","domain":1,"text_native":"Како сте? Kako ste?","text_romanized":"KAH-koh steh?","text_english":"How are you?","source_caption":"How are you?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The opening move in almost every conversation. In most of these languages it is a greeting rather than a question and does not expect a literal answer.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Serbian phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbian_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"srp-t0-0006","lang":"srp","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.nice-to-meet-you","domain":1,"text_native":"Драго ми је. Drago mi je.","text_romanized":"DRAH-goh mee yeh","text_english":"Nice to meet you.","source_caption":"Pleased to meet you.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Said on a first introduction. In several languages there is a separate phrase for meeting someone formally that a stranger will use instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Serbian phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbian_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"srp-t0-0007","lang":"srp","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.what-is-your-name","domain":1,"text_native":"Како се зовете? Kako se zovete?","text_romanized":"KAH-koh seh ZOH-veh-teh","text_english":"What is your name?","source_caption":"What is your name?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"You get asked this before you get to ask it. Recognising the question is the difference between answering and freezing.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Serbian phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbian_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"srp-t0-0008","lang":"srp","tier":0,"slot":"courtesy.please","domain":1,"text_native":"Молим. Molim.","text_romanized":"MOH-leem","text_english":"Please.","source_caption":"Please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Not a filler in English, and a grammatical particle in some of these languages — one word that changes a sentence from an order to a request.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Serbian phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbian_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"srp-t0-0009","lang":"srp","tier":0,"slot":"courtesy.thank-you","domain":1,"text_native":"Хвала. Hvala.","text_romanized":"HVAH-lah","text_english":"Thank you.","source_caption":"Thank you.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The single most useful word in any of these languages. Saying it costs nothing and changes how everything after it is received.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Serbian phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbian_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"srp-t0-0010","lang":"srp","tier":0,"slot":"courtesy.excuse-me","domain":1,"text_native":"Извините. Izvinite.","text_romanized":"eez-VEE-nee-teh","text_english":"Excuse me.","source_caption":"Excuse me. (getting attention)","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Two different things in one phrase: getting someone's attention, and getting past them. Guessing wrong is jarring — one version walks through a conversation.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Serbian phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbian_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"srp-t0-0011","lang":"srp","tier":0,"slot":"courtesy.goodbye","domain":1,"text_native":"Довиђења. Doviđenja.","text_romanized":"doh vee-JEH-nyah","text_english":"Goodbye.","source_caption":"Goodbye","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"How you leave. Leaving without one is noticeably rude in most of these languages.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Serbian phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbian_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"srp-t0-0012","lang":"srp","tier":0,"slot":"repair.dont-understand","domain":12,"text_native":"Не разумем. Ne razumem.","text_romanized":"neh rah-ZOO-mehm","text_english":"I do not understand.","source_caption":"I don't understand.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The one phrase that keeps a conversation alive. Without it people stop trying, and with it they often rephrase in simpler words.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Serbian phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbian_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"srp-t0-0013","lang":"srp","tier":0,"slot":"repair.help-me","domain":12,"text_native":"Можете ли да ми помогнете молим вас?, Možete li da mi pomognete molim vas?","text_romanized":"MOH-zheh-teh lee dah mee POH-mohg-neh-teh MOH-leem vahs","text_english":"Can you help me, please?","source_caption":"Can you help me please?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The opener for every request that follows. Standing in front of someone not being asked anything is how people get ignored.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Serbian phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbian_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"srp-t0-0014","lang":"srp","tier":0,"slot":"bridge.speak-english","domain":12,"text_native":"Говорите ли енглески? Govorite li engleski?","text_romanized":"GOH-voh-ree-teh lee ENH-glehs-kee?","text_english":"Do you speak English?","source_caption":"Do you speak English?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Asked of you constantly, and the question that decides whether anything after it can happen. There is a polite version and a blunt version and the gap between them is wide.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Serbian phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Serbian_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
